================================================================================
Absorbed engine source (vendored, owned, NOT synced upstream)
================================================================================

UnieInfra is an agent-oriented inference engine that absorbs valuable components
from other inference engines as *owned in-tree source*, not as library
dependencies. Absorbed source is hard-forked: we do not merge, rebase or pull
from upstream. Each absorbed component records its own provenance and license
below; per-component detail lives next to the code.

  unieinfra-vllm/    vLLM (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm)
                     Apache License 2.0.
                     Hard fork at commit d02df748bf9efd99022f1a062597dc3cb3808485
                     (v0.13.0rc1-6959), snapshot dated 2026-07-24, vendored
                     2026-07-25. The upstream LICENSE is retained unmodified at
                     unieinfra-vllm/LICENSE and every upstream file keeps its
                     "SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM
                     project" header. Files UnieInfra changed are listed
                     individually in unieinfra-vllm/PROVENANCE.md, satisfying
                     Apache-2.0 section 4(b). The upstream README is preserved
                     as unieinfra-vllm/UPSTREAM_README.md. The Python import
                     package is still named `vllm`; this is a deliberate,
                     documented deferral of the rename, not a claim of identity
                     with upstream.

UnieInfra is NOT affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by the vLLM project
or its contributors.

Components under evaluation for absorption are tracked as git submodules under
third_party/ (see below) until they are actually vendored. A submodule is a
reference, not a dependency and not redistributed; a directory at the repository
root is absorbed source that we own.

================================================================================
Vendored third-party components
================================================================================

TokenSpeed vendors third-party source under
tokenspeed-kernel/python/tokenspeed_kernel/thirdparty/. Each retains its own
upstream copyright and license; refer to the headers within these directories
and to the corresponding upstream projects for terms:

  - cuda/       hand-written CUDA kernels, incl. FlashInfer-derived headers
  - cute_dsl/   NVIDIA CuTe DSL kernels
  - deep_gemm/  DeepGEMM
  - msa/        MiniMax sparse attention (CUTLASS-derived)
  - triton/     Triton kernels
  - trtllm/     TensorRT-LLM-derived kernels

================================================================================
Reference-only dependencies (NOT vendored, NOT redistributed)
================================================================================

The following live as git submodules under third_party/ for reference and
interoperability work only. They are not part of the UnieInfra distribution and
retain their own licenses:

  - third_party/vllm     — vLLM            (Apache-2.0) — kept at the pin
                           d02df748 that unieinfra-vllm/ was vendored from, so
                           the fork's provenance stays verifiable
  - third_party/sglang   — SGLang           (Apache-2.0)
  - third_party/FastVideo — FastVideo       (Apache-2.0)
  - third_party/JetSpec  — JetSpec          (MIT)
  - third_party/lmdeploy — LMDeploy         (Apache-2.0)
  - third_party/TensorRT-LLM — TensorRT-LLM (Apache-2.0)
  - third_party/modular  — Modular/Mojo/MAX (Apache-2.0 with LLVM exceptions)
  - third_party/tilert   — TileRT           (see third_party/tilert/LICENSE)

If any of these is later absorbed as source, it moves out of third_party/, gains
its own PROVENANCE record, and is listed in the "Absorbed engine source" section
above with its commit and license — not merely acknowledged here.
